Z||000000||GT Bastard||03-09-2000||05:39 PM||||Hey everybody, I've got a question for all you V6 owners. My father is heavily into performance cars and has taken an interest in our plastic friend. He has the knowledge and the facilities to fabricate an entirely new "performance oriented" intake for the V6 models. All I know so far is that it will have shorter runners than the factory intake. Who would be interested in a whole new aluminum intake with shorter runners? What else would you like this intake to have? He did say that he plans on adapting the factory throttle body to it in case you're wondering. The shorter runners may cause some low end torque to be reduced, but the gain in HP should easily offset it by his calculations(the trend seems to be moving in that direction when you look at the difference between old TPI motors vs. the LT1 and LS1.)  Give me some input on what you guys what this intake to have and whether or not you'd be interested.  We've also discussed porting a large number of existing manifolds, but that's less exciting! What do YOU think?||||reg||14
Z||000001||Carolina 88GT||03-09-2000||05:50 PM||||I might be very interested.  Have been slowly working up to an new air intake system.....but they are rather hard to come by.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
