Z||000014||FIEROCIOUS||03-10-2000||01:47 AM||||A upper plenum with tuned velocity stacks in side a main chamber (STR style) for civics. The throttle body will feed all six runners.<BR>The hard part is to tune the velocity stacks for each cylinder. EGR compatible would be nice also. I'd send pics but I don't have a scanner or camera! Will this be naturaly aspirated or a roots type blower set up? You need to deside.||||reg||1
Z||000015||Monkeyman||03-10-2000||05:44 AM||||What's the story with the aluminum heads?  I thought ours were cast iron.||||reg||1
Z||000016||batboy||03-10-2000||07:41 AM||||Of course Fieros have cast iron heads, but there are millions of GM front wheel drive cars out there that use the 3.1 engine with aluminum heads (which flow very good). Trouble is, the Fiero intake won't fit on these heads. If they can make an intake for these aluminum heads that will accept the Fiero fuel injection, then that would very much simplify an engine swap so that you don't have to change out the ECM and wiring. I like the idea!<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 03-10-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000017||1FieroGTRacingInc||03-10-2000||09:04 AM||||I'll want one too for a SuperCharger..   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000018||87SC/GT||03-10-2000||12:56 PM||||BTW, you don't want to supercharge or turbo with the aluminum head. They are very prone to cracking with the slightest overheating condition.(probably not a good choice for the fiero either) I'm not saying all aluminum heads are this way, but from my experience the 3.1 heads do not take abuse very well.<P> If we are going to use a blower, why not the WEIAND or B&M Mini-blower? Probably cheaper than the Eaton blower if you can even find one for sale. Salvage yards are not hip on splitting the blower from the motor. (At least not from my experience) <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000019||GT Bastard||03-10-2000||02:03 PM||||This is some good information.  Anymore ideas?  Getting my hands on a blower may not be easy, and I'm sure my father would want to have a working model to design the intake from, because I'm sure there isn't going to be any room for error.||||reg||1
Z||000020||Patrick's Dad||03-10-2000||10:16 PM||||Hi Guys,<P>I've been working on this one in my head (not an engineer, but willing to do a little trial and error). I'm a naturally aspirated kind of guy, and what I'll be trying in the mid to later stages of this rebuild is to put the Gen III Aluminum heads on the 3.4, and split the plenum to flow two throttle bodies; one into each bank of cylinders. I have some concepts down, others I'm still working on (Particularly sensors and ECM). Depending on the setup of this new intake, it may be modifiable to my project (Although this is projected to be 2-3 years away).||||reg||1
